02:15:50.890 --> 02:15:51.850
early

02:15:52.090 --> 02:15:57.665
to kind of spread that expense out. So it's not all a big hit in one year.

02:15:59.505 --> 02:16:05.345
You know, but overall, it's slightly cheaper over a, say, four year period to renegotiate

02:16:05.345 --> 02:16:09.905
early than it would be to wait until this contract extends

02:16:09.905 --> 02:16:14.470
and then deal with one really big jump. But we would be trading off

02:16:14.710 --> 02:16:19.190
more expense next year for less expense in future years.

02:16:19.750 --> 02:16:22.470
So if that's something the board wants to consider,

02:16:22.710 --> 02:16:24.790
we can consider renegotiating

02:16:24.790 --> 02:16:25.750
that for next year.

02:16:27.055 --> 02:16:30.334
